{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1116365-the-fading-forgetting-and-undoing-or-why-has-it-slipped-into-the-mists-in-c20","id":1116365,"title":"The Fading (Forgetting and Undoing) or why has it slipped into the Mists in C20?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-15T07:02:28-07:00","id":1116365,"title":"The Fading (Forgetting and Undoing) or why has it slipped into the Mists in C20?","content":"I just finished reading C20, and I was surprised, to say the least, to find that there is no section on the effects of Banality and the Mists on changelings. There is, sure, a new section on how the Mists may affect changelings whose Banality is higher than their Glamour, but nothing on the Fading, and its two manifestations, the Forgetting and the Undoing.<br /> <br /> There are some occurrences of these words (a quick search using the Tools in Acrobat help find them, since there is no Index... I hope there will be one in the printed book), for instance on p. 366 where the Fading is qualified as &quot;natural&quot; and the Undoing as &quot;unnatural&quot;, or on p. 337 on the fate of changelings who become Undone, but there is no section on clarifying the process of the Forgetting.<br /> <br /> The <b>Undoing </b>is simple enough: when a changeling reaches 10 permanent Banality, she is Undone, and I quite like the section on the Undone (p. 366).<br /> <br /> I had hoped that C20 would tackle once and for all this issue, because in previous editions, the Forgetting was always treated with some confusion.<br /> <br /> In Autumn People, a sidebar was devoted to the question (p. 32). It was reproduced in Book of Lost Dreams (p. 37). (Which was astonishing: why were these very important rules not included in the core book?) Problem: the text was confusing.<br /> <br /> The <b>Forgetting </b>could occur on three different occasions (I summarize the original texts):<br /> <br /> 1) &quot;<i>Banality higher than Glamour: The Kithain is in danger of temporary memory loss whenever her Banality is greater than her Glamour. This generally begins to occur after a story is over, and can take days to week, depending on the Storyteller\u2019s discretion\u2026 Roll Glamour against the Kithain\u2019s Banality each time the Kithain is not actively touched by Glamour. </i><i>Failure means falling into the Mists.</i> <i>She can, of course, be drawn out of it by another Kithain.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I interpret this as follow: whenever a changeling's <b>temporary </b>Banality is greater than her <b>permanent </b>Glamour, she may succumb to the Mists. Roll the changeling's permanent Glamour against her permanent Banality each time she is not actively touched by Glamour. Failure means falling into the Mists, i.e. she gets a dot of Banality (see below for the reasoning beyond this), she forgets her fae nature and lives a mortal life, thereby risking to acquire more Banality. Once the time determined by the Mists Charts have elapsed, then, and only then can other changelings draw her out by giving her Glamour (but only if they are from the same oathcircle, because I seem to remember that only in this case are changelings able to share Glamour) or bringing her to a freehold or she stumbles upon a source of Glamour (a trod opening, another changeling's Chrysalis, etc.).<br /> <br /> In C20 there is a new rule which applies to this situation: a changeling possessing a Treasure never fears to forget her fae nature.<br /> <br /> <i>2) &quot;Banality Above Glamour and Willpower: whenever permanent Banality exceeds both permanent Glamour and Willpower, the Kithain is in danger of the Forgetting... For each dot that the Kithain has over his Glamour rating, she should spend at least one day in a freehold (or in the Dreaming, or being actively involved in the Dreaming) to offset the effects of high Banality. If she does not, she risks reverting back to her seeming, and gains one point of Banality each week this requirement is not met.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Here it is fairly straightforward. Maybe this rule should be replaced now by the new rule on the Mists effects (p. 270 in C20).<br /> <br /> 3) Finally there is a last occurrence when a changeling falls into the Forgetting: by being chimerically killed. In C20, a chimerical death plunges a changeling into the Mists and gives her half her Banality rating in points of Banality. While it was only said so in the FAQ on the old WW website, being chimerically killed earned the changeling a dot of Banality and the loss of all her Glamour points as she fell into the Mists. This is why I think that a changeling who has fallen into the Mists should &quot;gain&quot; a dot in Banality.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","user":"mattboggan","date":". 07-15-2017, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T00:25:54-07:00","id":1116753,"title":"","content":"Personally I think that the C20 rules on Mists, the ones on p.270, could just replace previous rules on Forgetting. No need to overcomplicate things. And similarly I do think that the C20 rules on Chimerical death are quite enough, I always thought that permanent Banality was a bit too much considering all the other effects of Chimerical death so this is a welcome change for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}